---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Barstool Sports at Shear Media Studios — REMI Case Study"
  description="How Pete Guzzo built the broadcast infrastructure, REMI workflow, and SRT transmission capability that brought Barstool Sports to Shear Media Studios — and kept them coming back every week."
  image="/images/studios/Shear-Media-Studios-Control-Room.jpg"
>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="cs-hero">
    <div class="cs-hero-inner">
      <a href="/work" class="cs-back">← Back to Work</a>
      <p class="cs-eyebrow">Case Study · Broadcast Infrastructure · Client Development</p>
      <h1 class="cs-h1">How I Built the Infrastructure That Brought Barstool Sports to Tampa Bay</h1>
      <p class="cs-hero-sub">Strategy. REMI workflow. SRT transmission. Six cameras in 4K to a control room in Chicago — and a recurring weekly client in the first six months.</p>
      <div class="cs-hero-meta">
        <div class="cs-meta-item"><span class="cs-meta-label">Client</span><span class="cs-meta-val">Shear Enterprises / Shear Media Studios</span></div>
        <div class="cs-meta-item"><span class="cs-meta-label">Role</span><span class="cs-meta-val">EVP — Strategy, Studio Operations & Business Development</span></div>
        <div class="cs-meta-item"><span class="cs-meta-label">Facility</span><span class="cs-meta-val">Shear Media Studios, St. Petersburg, FL</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-hero-globe">
      <img src="/images/studios/SMS-SRT-Transmission-Globe.png" alt="SRT transmission from Tampa Bay to control rooms in Chicago, London, Toronto and Sydney" class="cs-globe-img" loading="eager" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROOF STRIP -->
  <section class="cs-proof">
    <div class="cs-proof-inner">
      <div class="cs-proof-stat"><span class="cs-stat-num">6</span><span class="cs-stat-label">Cameras in 4K</span></div>
      <div class="cs-proof-stat"><span class="cs-stat-num">4</span><span class="cs-stat-label">Continents reached</span></div>
      <div class="cs-proof-stat"><span class="cs-stat-num">52+</span><span class="cs-stat-label">Weeks, recurring</span></div>
      <div class="cs-proof-stat"><span class="cs-stat-num">0</span><span class="cs-stat-label">Shows missed</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE SITUATION -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-light">
    <div class="cs-container cs-two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">The situation</p>
        <h2 class="cs-h2">A new facility. No national broadcast clients. No proven workflow.</h2>
        <p class="cs-body">When I joined Shear Enterprises as EVP, Shear Media Studios existed as a building. It didn't yet have the infrastructure, the market positioning, or the client relationships to attract a recurring national broadcast production.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">Barstool Sports wasn't a client. The REMI workflow didn't exist. The Appear X20 wasn't installed. The booking and operations system that protects a recurring client's time in the building — that didn't exist either.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">I was hired to build all of it. And to go get the clients before the ink was dry.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-img-block">
        <img src="/images/studios/Shear-Media-Studios-Control-Room.jpg" alt="Shear Media Studios broadcast control room" class="cs-img" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE STRATEGY -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">The strategy</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">Build the capability before the client exists. Position the facility for clients most studios never see.</h2>
      <div class="cs-body-wide">
        <p class="cs-body">Most facilities wait for a client to ask before they build. I've never worked that way.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">I identified the client profiles that would differentiate Shear from every other production studio in Tampa Bay: sports networks, niche content series, recurring broadcast productions, national brands that needed a turnkey technical home in a market they couldn't staff full-time.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">Tampa Bay is significantly underserved as a production market relative to its sports infrastructure, its population, and its geographic position. That's not a liability — it's a positioning advantage. Florida has no state income tax. There are 35+ professional and college sports teams within two hours. The Gulf Coast is an underexplored origination point for networks that already have Chicago and New York covered.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">I built the pitch around that. Then I built the tech that made the pitch real.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-pillars">
        <div class="cs-pillar"><span class="cs-pillar-n">01</span><h3 class="cs-pillar-title">Infrastructure first</h3><p class="cs-pillar-body">Designed the broadcast control room, REMI workflow, and booking/operations system before going to market.</p></div>
        <div class="cs-pillar"><span class="cs-pillar-n">02</span><h3 class="cs-pillar-title">Positioned for the right clients</h3><p class="cs-pillar-body">Sports networks, specialty series, podcast creators, broadcast nationals — not the generic local event market.</p></div>
        <div class="cs-pillar"><span class="cs-pillar-n">03</span><h3 class="cs-pillar-title">Developed the relationships</h3><p class="cs-pillar-body">Built the technical demonstration capability and closed Barstool as a recurring weekly production partner.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE TECH -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-light">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">The technology</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">Broadcast-grade contribution infrastructure. Not a consumer encoder. Not a cloud stream.</h2>
      <div class="cs-tech-grid">
        <div class="cs-tech-block">
          <h3 class="cs-tech-title">REMI — Remote Integration Model</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">REMI is how major networks produce live sports and news from a remote site without sending a production truck. Talent and cameras at the venue — in this case, Studio G at Shear Media Studios. Director, switcher, and graphics at the network's home control room.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">Six cameras originate in St. Petersburg. They travel in 4K to the production control room in real time. Program and confidence feeds come back to the studio floor. The show is cut at the network's home base while the production runs live in Tampa Bay.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-tech-block">
          <h3 class="cs-tech-title">SRT Transmission · Appear X20</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Contribution at Shear Media Studios runs on the Appear X20 — the same modular broadcast processing platform network engineers already run in their own plant. It's a 2RU modular chassis built for SDI, IP and hybrid workflows. It is not a consumer encoder.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">When a network's ingest receives the feed from Studio G, it receives a signal the X20 was designed to send. Codec, transport and redundancy parameters are confirmed on the technical pre-call.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-tech-block">
          <h3 class="cs-tech-title">ISO Recording + Returns</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">While six cameras transmit to the remote control room for the live line cut, ISO cameras record locally at Shear Media Studios simultaneously. The production gets the live cut and the isolated camera recordings for post.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-tech-block">
          <h3 class="cs-tech-title">The Transmission Test</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Before the first show went live, we had to prove the system would hold. No static IP on our end. Our network team hit a wall. Five engineers were waiting on the other end.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">I paired the AI agents I'd been building for months with Codex, worked through our network documentation in real time, and extracted what we needed. The connection held. The show went live.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- REMI VS STREAMING -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark cs-compare">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">REMI vs. Streaming</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">Two different pipes. Shear Media Studios does both.</h2>
      <div class="cs-compare-grid">
        <div class="cs-compare-col cs-compare-remi">
          <h3 class="cs-compare-head">REMI sends</h3>
          <ul class="cs-compare-list">
            <li>Every camera, individually</li>
            <li>To a control room, for a director</li>
            <li>In real time — the network cuts live</li>
            <li>Program and confidence returns to the floor</li>
            <li>Broadcast ingest on the receiving end</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-compare-col cs-compare-stream">
          <h3 class="cs-compare-head">A live stream sends</h3>
          <ul class="cs-compare-list">
            <li>One finished program feed</li>
            <li>To a platform, for viewers</li>
            <li>With a few seconds of delay</li>
            <li>No return path needed</li>
            <li>CDN on the receiving end</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="cs-compare-note">Most studios can do the second. Shear Media Studios does both, from the same floor, on the same day.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- DESTINATIONS -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-light">
    <div class="cs-container cs-destinations">
      <div>
        <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">Where we reach</p>
        <h2 class="cs-h2">Any control room with a broadcast ingest. Any platform with an RTMP endpoint.</h2>
        <p class="cs-body">The Barstool production connects Tampa Bay to Chicago every week. The same path runs to London, Toronto, Sydney, or any other control room. Same workflow, different destination.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">For live streaming: YouTube, TikTok Live, Instagram Live, Twitch, LinkedIn Live, Facebook, or a private event platform. Multi-camera, graphics, lower thirds, remote guests — one stream or several platforms at once.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-dest-list">
        <div class="cs-dest-item"><span class="cs-dest-city">Chicago</span><span class="cs-dest-note">Current REMI partner — Barstool Sports weekly production</span></div>
        <div class="cs-dest-item"><span class="cs-dest-city">London</span><span class="cs-dest-note">Broadcast contribution, UK networks</span></div>
        <div class="cs-dest-item"><span class="cs-dest-city">Toronto</span><span class="cs-dest-note">Canadian broadcast contribution</span></div>
        <div class="cs-dest-item"><span class="cs-dest-city">Sydney</span><span class="cs-dest-note">Australian broadcast contribution</span></div>
        <div class="cs-dest-item"><span class="cs-dest-city">Any platform</span><span class="cs-dest-note">YouTube · TikTok Live · Instagram · Twitch · LinkedIn · Facebook</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE RESULT -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">The result</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">A national sports network client in the first six months. A full production ecosystem built on the same infrastructure.</h2>
      <div class="cs-result-grid">
        <div class="cs-result-block">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title">Barstool Sports</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Recurring weekly professional football production at Studio G. Custom set built specifically for the show. Six cameras in 4K to Chicago every week. Never missed a show.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-block">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title">Podcast + Creator Studios</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Five podcast configurations, any of them a live source. From solo creator to full broadcast crew, without friction.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-block">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title">Specialty Series</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Niche sports programming, content series, and brands that needed a turnkey production home in a market they couldn't staff full-time.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-block">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title">The Principle</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">The building works because it was built to work before the client asked for it. The same strategy and the same infrastructure behind every client that followed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-light">
    <div class="cs-container cs-faq-wrap">
      <div>
        <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">Questions</p>
        <h2 class="cs-h2">On the infrastructure and the workflow</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-faq">
        <details class="cs-faq-item">
          <summary class="cs-faq-q">What is REMI?</summary>
          <p class="cs-faq-a">Remote Integration Model: cameras and talent at a remote site — Shear Media Studios in St. Petersburg — and the director, switcher and graphics at the network's home control room. Every camera travels to the control room in real time; the network cuts the show there; program and confidence feeds come back to the floor here.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="cs-faq-item">
          <summary class="cs-faq-q">Is this the same as a livestream?</summary>
          <p class="cs-faq-a">No. A stream sends one finished picture to a platform, on a delay, with no return path. A REMI send delivers every camera individually, in real time, to a control room for live switching, with return video to the floor. The receiving end is a broadcast ingest, not a CDN. We do both.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="cs-faq-item">
          <summary class="cs-faq-q">What resolution and frame rate?</summary>
          <p class="cs-faq-a">4K at broadcast frame rates. Codec and transport parameters are confirmed on the technical pre-call with your network engineer.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="cs-faq-item">
          <summary class="cs-faq-q">Can you do this from a venue?</summary>
          <p class="cs-faq-a">Yes. The same contribution path runs from a venue or arena. Talk to us about the location and lead time.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="cs-faq-item">
          <summary class="cs-faq-q">What's the latency to our control room?</summary>
          <p class="cs-faq-a">Determined by the contribution path and confirmed on the technical pre-call with your network engineer.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="cs-faq-item">
          <summary class="cs-faq-q">Can you stream to more than one platform at once?</summary>
          <p class="cs-faq-a">Yes. Destinations and stream configuration are confirmed before show day.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark cs-cta-section">
    <div class="cs-container cs-cta-inner">
      <h2 class="cs-cta-head">Have a production that needs this kind of infrastructure?</h2>
      <p class="cs-cta-sub">I build studios and production systems that work at this level. If you need the strategy, the tech, or both — let's talk.</p>
      <div class="cs-cta-btns">
        <a href="/contact" class="cs-btn-primary">Talk to Pete →</a>
        <a href="https://www.shearmediastudios.com/live-transmission" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cs-btn-secondary">Book a technical call at SMS →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ─── TOKENS ─── */
  :root {
    --cs-ink: #1c1917;
    --cs-paper: #f5f0eb;
    --cs-rust: #9b4a2a;
    --cs-dark-bg: #0d0f14;
    --cs-dark-surface: #151820;
    --cs-dark-border: rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
    --cs-dark-text: #e8e2da;
    --cs-dark-muted: rgba(232,226,218,0.60);
    --cs-accent: #5ea8e6;
    --cs-accent-warm: #f1f6a4;
    --cs-container: 72rem;
    --cs-px: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  /* ─── HERO ─── */
  .cs-hero {
    background: var(--cs-dark-bg);
    color: var(--cs-dark-text);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    max-width: var(--cs-container);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem var(--cs-px) 5rem;
  }
  .cs-back {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--cs-dark-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }
  .cs-back:hover { color: var(--cs-dark-text); }
  .cs-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--cs-accent-warm);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .cs-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.2vw, 2.75rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: #fff;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }
  .cs-hero-sub {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--cs-dark-muted);
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .cs-hero-meta { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .cs-meta-item { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .cs-meta-label { color: var(--cs-accent); font-weight: 600; min-width: 4rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-size: 0.7rem; padding-top: 0.05rem; }
  .cs-meta-val { color: var(--cs-dark-muted); }
  .cs-hero-globe { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
  .cs-globe-img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 480px;
    mix-blend-mode: lighten;
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, #000 58%, transparent 72%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, #000 58%, transparent 72%);
  }

  /* ─── PROOF STRIP ─── */
  .cs-proof {
    background: var(--cs-dark-surface);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border);
  }
  .cs-proof-inner {
    max-width: var(--cs-container);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem var(--cs-px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .cs-proof-stat { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; }
  .cs-stat-num { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 3rem); color: #fff; line-height: 1; }
  .cs-stat-label { font-size: 0.7rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: var(--cs-accent-warm); }

  /* ─── SECTIONS ─── */
  .cs-section { padding: 5rem 0; }
  .cs-light { background: var(--cs-paper); color: var(--cs-ink); }
  .cs-dark { background: var(--cs-dark-bg); color: var(--cs-dark-text); }
  .cs-container { max-width: var(--cs-container); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--cs-px); }
  .cs-section-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .cs-light .cs-section-eyebrow { color: var(--cs-rust); }
  .cs-dark .cs-section-eyebrow { color: var(--cs-accent-warm); }
  .cs-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.8vw, 2.25rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
  .cs-light .cs-h2 { color: var(--cs-ink); }
  .cs-dark .cs-h2 { color: #fff; }
  .cs-body { font-size: 0.975rem; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .cs-light .cs-body { color: rgba(28,25,23,0.75); }
  .cs-dark .cs-body { color: var(--cs-dark-muted); }
  .cs-body-wide { max-width: 46rem; }

  /* ─── TWO-COL ─── */
  .cs-two-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4rem; align-items: center; }
  .cs-img-block { border-radius: 0.5rem; overflow: hidden; }
  .cs-img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }

  /* ─── PILLARS ─── */
  .cs-pillars { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 2rem; margin-top: 3rem; }
  .cs-pillar { border-top: 2px solid var(--cs-dark-border); padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  .cs-pillar-n { font-size: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: var(--cs-accent); font-weight: 700; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .cs-pillar-title { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: 1.05rem; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .cs-pillar-body { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--cs-dark-muted); }

  /* ─── TECH GRID ─── */
  .cs-tech-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .cs-tech-block { border-top: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.12); padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  .cs-tech-title { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--cs-ink); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }

  /* ─── COMPARE ─── */
  .cs-compare-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .cs-compare-col { border: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border); border-radius: 0.5rem; padding: 1.75rem 2rem; }
  .cs-compare-remi { border-color: rgba(94,168,230,0.4); background: rgba(94,168,230,0.04); }
  .cs-compare-head { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: 1rem; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 1rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .cs-compare-remi .cs-compare-head { color: var(--cs-accent); }
  .cs-compare-list { margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 1.1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .cs-compare-list li { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--cs-dark-muted); line-height: 1.5; }
  .cs-compare-note { margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 0.975rem; color: var(--cs-dark-muted); border-top: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border); padding-top: 1.5rem; font-style: italic; }

  /* ─── DESTINATIONS ─── */
  .cs-destinations { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4rem; align-items: start; }
  .cs-dest-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.12); }
  .cs-dest-item { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 8rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.08); align-items: baseline; }
  .cs-dest-city { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: 1rem; color: var(--cs-ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .cs-dest-note { font-size: 0.825rem; color: rgba(28,25,23,0.55); line-height: 1.5; }

  /* ─── RESULT ─── */
  .cs-result-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .cs-result-block { border-top: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border); padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  .cs-result-title { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--cs-accent-warm); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }

  /* ─── FAQ ─── */
  .cs-faq-wrap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr; gap: 4rem; align-items: start; }
  .cs-faq { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .cs-faq-item { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.10); }
  .cs-faq-q {
    font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 0.975rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    color: var(--cs-ink);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .cs-faq-q::after { content: '+'; font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--cs-rust); flex-shrink: 0; transition: transform 0.2s; }
  details[open] .cs-faq-q::after { transform: rotate(45deg); }
  .cs-faq-a { font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.7; color: rgba(28,25,23,0.65); padding-bottom: 1.1rem; margin: 0; }

  /* ─── CTA ─── */
  .cs-cta-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border); }
